{"id":"H5352","lemma":"נָקָה","transliteration":"naqah","sayIt":"na-QAH","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to clear","meaning":"1) to be empty, be clear, be pure, be free, be innocent, be desolate, be cut off\n1a) (Qal) to be empty, be clean, be pure\n1b) (Niphal)\n1b1) to be cleaned out, be purged out\n1b2) to be clean, be free from guilt, be innocent\n1b3) to be free, be exempt from punishment\n1b4) to be free, be exempt from obligation\n1c) (Piel)\n1c1) to hold innocent, acquit\n1c2) to leave unpunished","glosses":["go unpunished","leave the guilty unpunished","leave anyone unpunished","acquit me","leave you unpunished","then you are released"],"count":33,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"gen-24","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"then you are released","kjv":"then thou shalt be clear"}},{"chapterId":"gen-24","v":41,"renderings":{"kjv":"Then shalt thou be clear"}},{"chapterId":"exo-20","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"leave anyone unpunished","kjv":"will not hold him guiltless"}},{"chapterId":"exo-21","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"shall go unpunished","kjv":"him be quit"}},{"chapterId":"exo-34","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"leave the guilty unpunished","kjv":"and that will by no means"}},{"chapterId":"num-5","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"may you be immune","kjv":"be thou free"}},{"chapterId":"num-5","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be unaffected","kjv":"then she shall be free"}},{"chapterId":"num-5","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be free","kjv":"be guiltless"}},{"chapterId":"num-14","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"leave the guilty unpunished","kjv":"and by no means"}},{"chapterId":"deu-5","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"leave anyone unpunished","kjv":"will not hold him guiltless"}},{"chapterId":"jdg-15","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"I will be blameless","kjv":"shall I be more blameless"}},{"chapterId":"1sa-26","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"and be guiltless","kjv":"and be guiltless"}},{"chapterId":"1ki-2","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"hold him guiltless","kjv":"Now therefore hold him not